  "full_response": "Core Git Concepts\n\nCategory: Git Best Practices / API Cheatsheet\n\nModule: ConceptsSubsection: Branching and Merging Internals Under the Hood\n\nThrough the branching and merging mechanisms. When you:\n\n1. Create a branch, Git creates light-weight (reference) object.\n2. Merge branch A into branch B, Git performs a three-way merge of the copy of branch A that branch B has with the main tree and branch B’s copy at the new tip of B.\n\nBranches are really references to commits. There are the the ‘main’ and the ‘HEAD’ so for each branch Git creates a copy reference pointing to head and another pointing to main. Munge to get this context really quthere is a original although. Two fine for most understand.\n\nA Devs default will be “main” which are the default checked out the branch in Git BASH CLI. You can follow all of this Git documentation Codelens of explanation here for more context https://git-scm.com/book/en/Git-Branching-Basics-eHgAJ\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: Git Best Practices / API Cheatsheet\n\nModule: Concepts\n\nSubsection: More Branch Internals\n\nWhen you branch, Git copies the reference pointer to the parent the checksum of the parent commit excluding the object Knx1umTdSbKFTAFXtbzkZ3sMqXSsYgsSpXisZ5B3xtIVRu which is stored in an object called, HEAD before the its reference was created there used to be only a small branch name but Git1021, the next version of makes this into an object that has 3 parts, some of it detailed here https://git-wiki.kernel.org/gitlist#In-depth_Branch_Structure_-_Simplified\n\nAdvancing that, merging is really a 3-way merge. A three-way merge actually performs a diff between of the last two commits per this, merge target, merge source and merge base eg: Merging ‘HEAD’ into ‘master’, 3-way Merge of HEAD commit, master-previous-commit and master-commit it creates with Git. It’s fresh full documentation of this here https://git-scm.com/en/Git-Branching-Collaboration-Branches-depth1WaApgVx1Q4cp1\n\nWhere else, which is a normally the most include git-brain and git-fastpath. Remember: In Git, branches are not just the destination of actions like checkout or merge. Any reference",
